WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:09.039
I really need to say a major and huge thank
you to our YouTube subscribers who now number

00:00:09.039 --> 00:00:16.960
more than 750,000 this happened yesterday,
so we're just past that number 750,000 now.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:19.670
And I'm just flattered and so inspired.

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:24.980
When we first started this channel, I think
in the first month we had four subscribers,

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:25.980
maybe it was 10.

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:33.660
I struggle to remember we now are gaining
several hundred subscribers every single day.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:38.230
And it's extremely exciting as we now get
into an election year, which is often when

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:43.329
growth accelerates and we are really positioned
to get to the next level.

00:00:43.329 --> 00:00:46.490
I mean in the YouTube left, thanks to your
support.

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:48.100
And I'm talking about the trolls as well.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:51.200
I'm thanking the trolls as well and I'll detail
that in a second.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:55.670
You've got the young Turks with four and a
half million subscribers and then you have

00:00:55.670 --> 00:01:01.579
the David Pakman show, Kyle Kalinsky and Sam
Cedar all in the 700 to 800,000 subscriber

00:01:01.579 --> 00:01:03.550
range, so this is a great place to be.

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:07.729
It's great company to share and now let me
get to the trolls and the haters.

00:01:07.729 --> 00:01:09.539
I have to thank them as well.

00:01:09.539 --> 00:01:15.170
The trolls and the haters who make it a point
to dislike my videos and leave a whole bunch

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:17.259
of hate comments on them.

00:01:17.259 --> 00:01:20.679
You are actually a huge part of the success
as well.

00:01:20.679 --> 00:01:23.689
Individually, the trolls are really annoying.

00:01:23.689 --> 00:01:31.069
In total, the trolls represent a portion of
the engagement on the channel that has helped

00:01:31.069 --> 00:01:33.939
us grow, dislikes count as engagement.

00:01:33.939 --> 00:01:37.909
You see a video and you were motivated to
dislike it.

00:01:37.909 --> 00:01:41.259
That means you're engaging with the content,
negative, angry comments.

00:01:41.259 --> 00:01:46.719
While many of the comments are vial in their
content, they are engagement and they say

00:01:46.719 --> 00:01:52.240
to the YouTube algorithm, wow, the content
here is getting people to take action.

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:57.030
The frequency with which someone is liking
or disliking or leaving a comment, that is

00:01:57.030 --> 00:02:02.419
a huge piece of the YouTube algorithm learning
whose videos are likely to generate a reaction

00:02:02.419 --> 00:02:04.329
and discussion and keep people watching.

00:02:04.329 --> 00:02:09.229
So genuinely thank you not only to the supporters
but to the trolls as well.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:13.390
All those comments saying, David, you're cha,
you're showing your channel are dying.

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:18.860
Your show is circling the drain by leaving
me those comments and by disliking my videos

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:22.240
you're helping to ensure that it's not the
case and that the show keeps growing.

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:26.790
So extraordinarily exciting year coming up
is my prediction.

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:31.960
As of right now, we are sort of projected
based on current subscriber growth rates to

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:35.970
be close to a million subscribers around election
2020.

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:43.160
Now my hope is that as we really get into
the 2020 election primaries, Trump on hinged,

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:48.240
all of that stuff, I hope that our growth
rate will accelerate slightly and push the

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:51.830
1 million subscriber milestone to before the
2020 election.

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:52.830
It would be amazing.

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:59.640
It is a stretch, but it would be amazing for
us to be a 1 million plus subscriber YouTube

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:04.090
channel, uh, by the time that we'd get to
the 2020 election.

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:08.540
And you know, in the end, the truth is really
what matters is views cause you don't have

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:10.980
to be subscribed to view the content.

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:15.260
Some people often tell me, you know, David,
Dave Rubin's YouTube channel is so much more

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:16.290
successful than yours.

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:18.250
He's got a million subscribers.

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:20.890
We have roughly doubled the views of Dave
Rubin's channel.

00:03:20.890 --> 00:03:25.080
Uh, and that is really, um, uh, the, the,
the most important thing.

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:30.250
But there's no question that subscribers are
sort of a very front and center barometer

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:31.570
for how a channel is doing.

00:03:31.570 --> 00:03:33.380
So we're going to continue doing our thing.

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:36.730
Seven 50 feels like a great number to be at
this point in time.

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:42.040
I look forward to continuing on in 2020 with
more content, more long form pieces, more

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:46.180
daily political news, interviews and everything
else that's been working for us so far.

